## X-Embeds: LibStub, LibEditMode

# One TOC for every flavour: Retail, Classic Era, the Anniversary realms,
# Mists Classic, Titan and WoW Forever, in that order above. Every number is
# kept current by .github/workflows/toc-interface.yml, which puts back any it
# cannot fetch, and tools/check-api-contract.sh also reports when Forever's is
# behind the client. The addon reads what it needs from the client at runtime
# and stands down per feature where a client lacks it (no combined window, no
# addon compartment, no Edit Mode), so the Lua is the same everywhere; the
# contract script checks each flavour's source.

# Uncomment and fill in to publish to another site. The packager skips any site
# whose ID is absent, even when its API token is set.
#   WoWInterface -- the number in wowinterface.com/downloads/infoNNNNN-Name
# ## X-WoWI-ID: 00000
#   Wago Addons -- the ID on the project page
# ## X-Wago-ID: 000000

# Order matters: Locales fills the string table the others read; each Core
# module publishes what the next one captures; MoveMyBags.Kuro.lua assembles the
# API that Options and EditMode read. Bindings.xml is picked up by the client
# by name and is not listed here. The libraries ship unmodified under Libs/
# (see Libs/LibEditMode/VENDORED.txt). LibEditMode hooks Edit Mode's frames
# the moment it loads, so it is gated to the game types its own TOC supports,
# and EditMode.lua reports it absent everywhere else.
Libs\LibStub\LibStub.lua
Libs\LibEditMode\embed.xml [AllowLoadGameType mainline, standard, camelot, tbc, mists]
Locales.lua
Core\Util.lua
Core\Storage.lua
Core\Layers.lua
Core\Trace.lua
Core\Layout.lua
Core\Drag.lua
Core\Commands.lua
MoveMyBags.Kuro.lua
Options.lua
EditMode.lua
